# This Python client does not auto-load .env: export the token through systemd,
# Docker or the invoking shell. The token is OPTIONAL: every A.R.M.O.R. repository
# is public, so remote discovery, install and update work without one; a token only
# raises GitHub's request ceiling (and is needed for a private fork of the ecosystem).
# Use a fine-grained personal access token with read-only access - nothing more.
# Never put a real token in this example or commit a local .env file.

GITHUB_TOKEN=
